                     <title ref="LIT0049IHA#s15IHA"/>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#iv">-iv</locus>وَلَوْ أَنَّنَا نَزَّلْنَا إِلَيْهِمِ [هكذا] المَلَىكَةَ وَكَلَّمَهُمُ المَوْتَى وَحَشَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ كُلَّ شَئٍّ</incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#9r">-9r</locus>فَاُصْبِرُوا حَتَّى يَحْكُمَ اللهُ بَيْنَنَا وَهْوَ خَيْرُ الحَكِمِيْنَ</explicit>
                     <note>6:111-7:87. Penciled pagination. The copyist did not complete his task. No sūra titles. No verse markers. Folios following 2r have only their 3 last lines vocalized. In the non-vocalized parts of the text, the upper stroke of kāf-s is missing. In the vocalized parts the letter is completed with a mark of ihmāl in a shape of a kāf. Thirteen lines a page. Catchwords probably by the same copyist.</note>
                     <note/>
